# A110.2 kernel desktop info line (sd-base, no #Z). The C:\ window is open at
# boot; its info line shows the whole directory (STINFOST). Ticks are 200 Hz
# after "[desk] desktop up" armed the injector. The pointer is parked at the
# bottom-right corner before every dump so the cursor never sits on the line.
# A: idle                 -> " <bytes> bytes used in <n> items."
# B: one icon clicked     -> STINFST2 with 1 selected item
# C: rubber band over the last row's two icons -> STINFST2 with 2
# D: click on empty space -> desk_clear -> back to STINFOST
200 parkbr
1000 arm
1100 mark A_IDLE
1400 move 95 105
1600 down
1603 up
1800 parkbr
2200 mark B_ONE_SELECTED
2500 move 70 340
2700 down
2750 drag 220 255
2900 up
3100 parkbr
3500 mark C_BAND_TWO
3800 move 400 340
4000 down
4003 up
4200 parkbr
4600 mark D_DESELECTED
